def the_firstborns_double(case, data):
    """F7 — Deut 21:15-17 — ONE LINE firstborn_portion_declared writing firstborn_double_portion_commanded (a STATUS) and firstborn_right_transfer_barred (a BLOCK); Genesis 48's portion and gift by CALL (family), Reuben's first of my strength by CALL (family), Zelophehad's ladder by CALL (zelophehad), Esau's birthright sold by CALL (mamre), the firstling from the womb by CALL (release_firstborn); the exam rows Bekhorot 8:1, 8:9 and Bava Batra 8:5 read whole"""
    del P_[:]
    ask = case['ask']
    if ask == 'two_wives_loved_and_hated':
        ink('21:15-16', '"IF A MAN HAS TWO WIVES, THE ONE LOVED AND THE OTHER HATED, and they bear him sons, the loved and the hated, AND THE FIRSTBORN SON IS THE HATED ONE\'S — then on the day he gives his sons inheritance of what he has, he may not make the loved one\'s son firstborn before the hated one\'s son, the firstborn" — "two wives" Lamech\'s phrase (Genesis 4:19 in the Torah; the reading\'s find — %d tokens in order shared; the tape\'s married lines at 4:19 the readback\'s REFERENCE); the parser %s at 21:15 (two, the one, the one), the starred tokens %s; "hated" Leah\'s word (Genesis 29:31, 29:33 — the tape\'s womb_opened the readback\'s REFERENCE; hated THREE on the-sons a different seat)' % (TWIN['21:15 vs Gen 4:19'], PARSE[(21, 15)][0], PARSE[(21, 15)][2]))
        move('the Sifrei 215:4-14, 216:1-4 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH BEKHOROT 8:1 (the exam row, read whole); cold_run_zelophehad (CALL) — ZL.inheritance_order(source_of_rule) = %s; cold_run_release_firstborn (CALL) — RF.the_firstling(consecrated_from_the_womb) = %s; cold_run_mamre (CALL) — MR.twins(firstborn_sheet) = %s' % (ZL_SRC[0][:30], RF_WOMB[1], MR_SHEET[0]), "'ONE LOVED AND ONE HATED' — hated in her marriage (a forbidden union) or hated by her husband: the arms (215:6); 'AND THEY BEAR HIM SONS' — sons, not daughters: the daughters excluded from the double (216:1-2 — zelophehad's ladder by CALL, the rule from the output not the plea); MISHNAH BEKHOROT 8:1 — THE FIRSTBORN FOR INHERITANCE AND NOT FOR THE PRIEST: he who came after a miscarriage whose head came out alive, after a nine-months' child whose head came out dead, after a beast-shaped miscarriage — R. Meir, the sages requiring a human form; the sandal, the afterbirth, the shaped sac, the cut-up; FOR THE PRIEST AND NOT FOR INHERITANCE: the man who had sons and married a woman who had none; the convert or the freed maidservant who conceived before; the uncertain births; the woman who did not wait three months; FOR BOTH: after the sac of water, of blood, of flesh, the fish-shaped, the fortieth day; FOR NEITHER — R. Yose the Galilean: 'whatever opens the womb among the children of Israel' (Exodus 13:2): the priest's firstborn is the womb's (release_firstborn by CALL), the inheritance's is the father's; Esau the first to come out (mamre by CALL — firstborn_by_the_head the tape's reference)")
        dat("THE PARAMETER the_firstborns_kinds (Bekhorot 8:1 — for inheritance not the priest, for the priest not inheritance, for both, for neither); the hated wife's arms a DATA row; the exam's person the son born after a miscarriage whose head came out alive — the firstborn for inheritance and not for the priest: accepted for the inheritance")
        return out("two wives loved and hated (21:15-16) — sons not daughters; the inheritance's firstborn the father's first, the priest's the womb's, four kinds (the Sifrei 215:4-216:4; Mishnah Bekhorot 8:1; zelophehad's rule, release_firstborn's %s and mamre's %s by CALL): the son after the miscarriage whose head came out alive accepted for the inheritance's firstborn" % (RF_WOMB[1][0], MR_SHEET[0]), ['accepted'])
    if ask == 'on_the_day_he_gives_his_sons_inheritance':
        ink('21:16', '"then ON THE DAY HE GIVES HIS SONS INHERITANCE of what he has, HE MAY NOT MAKE THE LOVED ONE\'S SON FIRSTBORN before the hated one\'s son, the firstborn" — the negation %s; "on the day" the judgment\'s hour (216:5)' % (NEG[(21, 16)],))
        move('the Sifrei 216:5, 217:1 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH BAVA BATRA 8:5 (the exam row, read whole); cold_run_family (CALL) — FA.inheritance(given_as_gift) = %s, (gift_returns_dispute) = %s, (held_not_due) = %s' % (FA_GIFT[0], FA_RET[0], FA_HELD[0]), "'ON THE DAY' — by day, not by night: the inheritance judged by day (216:5 — the English's note); MISHNAH BAVA BATRA 8:5 — 'my firstborn son shall not take double', 'my son shall not inherit with his brothers' — HE HAS SAID NOTHING, for he stipulated against what is written in the Torah; but he who divides his property by mouth on his deathbed — more to one and less to one, the firstborn made equal to them — his words stand; if he said 'as inheritance' he has said nothing; if he wrote 'as a gift' at the beginning, the middle or the end — his words stand (family's given_as_gift by CALL — Jacob's 'I have given you' the gift verb); R. Yochanan ben Beroka: about one fit to inherit his words stand; property written to others leaving his sons — done, but the sages are displeased; Rabban Simeon ben Gamliel: if the sons did not act properly, he is remembered for good (217:1 — the gift's channel the family runner's rows)")
        dat("THE WRITE firstborn_right_transfer_barred — a BLOCK on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DJ2); THE PARAMETER the_stipulation_against_the_torah (Bava Batra 8:5 — the inheritance form void, the gift form stands); the exam's person the father who says 'my firstborn shall not take double' — has said nothing: barred from the transfer; the father who gives by gift on his deathbed accepted")
        return out("on the day he gives his sons inheritance (21:16) — by day; the stipulation against the Torah void, the gift form stands (the Sifrei 216:5, 217:1; Mishnah Bava Batra 8:5; family's gift %s, the dispute %s and the held %s by CALL): THE WRITE firstborn_right_transfer_barred, a BLOCK on Israel at the chapters' own day; the father who says 'my firstborn shall not take double' barred from the transfer" % (FA_GIFT[0], FA_RET[0][0], FA_HELD[0]), ['firstborn_right_transfer_barred'])
    if ask == 'double_of_all_that_he_has':
        ink('21:17', '"but he shall acknowledge the firstborn, the hated one\'s son, TO GIVE HIM DOUBLE OF ALL THAT HE HAS, FOR HE IS THE FIRST OF HIS STRENGTH; THE RIGHT OF THE FIRSTBORN IS HIS" — the parser %s at 21:17 ("double" READ [2] — the reading\'s parser assert); "PI SHNAYIM" (double) at 21:17 and 17:6\'s "the mouth of two" ONE consonantal word (the reading\'s find — the homograph); "the first of his strength" at 21:17 and Genesis 49:3 ALONE (family\'s seats %s; the shared run %d — the vav\'s spelling the reading\'s find); "the right of the firstborn" the Bible\'s one seat' % (PARSE[(21, 17)][0], FA_STR[0], TWIN['21:17 vs Gen 49:3']))
        move('the Sifrei 217:2-8 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH BEKHOROT 8:9 (the exam row, read whole); cold_run_family (CALL) — FA.inheritance(one_portion) = %s, (birthright_run) = %s, FA.testament(firstborn_my_strength) = %s, (excess_named_denied) = %s; cold_run_zelophehad (CALL) — ZL.inheritance_order(firstborn_double) = %s; cold_run_mamre (CALL) — MR.twins(sale_with_oath) = %s' % (FA_ONE[0], FA_RUN[0], FA_STR[0], FA_EXC[0], ZL_DBL[1], MR_SALE[0]), "MISHNAH BEKHOROT 8:9 — the firstborn takes DOUBLE in the father's property and not in the mother's; not in the improvement after the death; NOT IN WHAT IS DUE AS IN WHAT IS HELD (ra'uy against muchzak — due against held: family's held_not_due by CALL, Genesis 48:22's 'which I took' the held); not the wife's marriage contract, not the daughters' maintenance, not the levirate brother; THE ARGUMENT FROM ONE AND FIVE BROTHERS — double of one brother's share, not of the whole estate, decided by 'of all that he has' (217:2-5 — Bava Batra 122b-123a the English's note, not read) and by JACOB'S ONE PORTION TO JOSEPH (Genesis 48:22 — the tape's portion_given the readback's REFERENCE; family's one portion and the birthright's run by CALL; 1 Chronicles 5:1 the birthright given to Joseph's sons — the Prophets' run citation); 'FOR HE IS THE FIRST OF HIS STRENGTH' — Reuben's (Genesis 49:3 — the tape's testament the readback's REFERENCE; family's first of my strength by CALL: the father's first, not the mother's — Bekhorot 8:1's two firstborns; the excess named and denied); 'THE RIGHT OF THE FIRSTBORN IS HIS' — through the judges (217:8); Esau's birthright sold with an oath (mamre by CALL — the birthright's earliest seat)")
        dat("THE WRITE firstborn_double_portion_commanded — a STATUS on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DJ2); THE PARAMETER the_doubles_measure (Bekhorot 8:9 — the father's, the held, one brother's share doubled, the exclusions); the homograph a DATA row; the exam's person the firstborn of six brothers — takes two of seven shares of the father's held property: portion_added the case's own body")
        return out("double of all that he has (21:17) — double in the father's held property, one brother's share doubled (one and five brothers), not the due, not the mother's; Jacob's one portion to Joseph and Reuben's first of my strength the tape's own seats; the birthright through the judges (the Sifrei 217:2-8; Mishnah Bekhorot 8:9; family's %s, %s and %s, zelophehad's %s and mamre's %s by CALL): THE WRITE firstborn_double_portion_commanded, a STATUS on Israel at the chapters' own day; the firstborn of six takes two of seven shares" % (FA_ONE[0][0], FA_RUN[0][0], FA_STR[0][0], ZL_DBL[1][0], MR_SALE[0][1]), ['firstborn_double_portion_commanded', 'portion_added'])
    return 'no verdict in span', [], list(P_)


def the_rebellious_son(case, data):
    """F8 — Deut 21:18-21 — ONE LINE rebellious_son_declared writing rebellious_son_seized_commanded and rebellious_son_stoning_commanded (STATUSES); the stoning rite by CALL (mekoshesh, seducers, courts_prophet), the three and the twenty-three by CALL (festivals_judges, ordinances); the window, the measures and the parents' conditions PARAMETERS graded by Sanhedrin 8:1-5 (the exam rows read whole); the son's own verdict stoned with the evil purged (the body effects reused)"""
    del P_[:]
    ask = case['ask']
    if ask == 'a_son_not_a_daughter':
        ink('21:18', '"IF A MAN HAS A STUBBORN AND REBELLIOUS SON, who hears not the voice of his father or the voice of his mother, and they chastise him and he will not hearken to them" — "stubborn and rebellious" at 21:18 and Jeremiah 5:23 alone (the reading\'s formula assert; %d shared — the heart alone); the negation %s' % (TWIN['21:18 vs Jer 5:23'], NEG[(21, 18)]))
        move('the Sifrei 218:1-3 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 8:1 (the exam row, read whole)', "MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 8:1: FROM WHEN is a stubborn and rebellious son liable? from when he brings forth two hairs until the beard is rounded — the lower and not the upper, but the sages spoke in a clean way; 'IF A MAN HAS A SON' — a son and not a daughter, a son and not a man; THE MINOR IS EXEMPT, for he has not come into the commandments (218:1-3); the three months of the window (Sanhedrin 69a — the English's note, not read)")
        dat("THE PARAMETER the_sons_window (Sanhedrin 8:1 — from two hairs until the beard rounds; a son, not a daughter, not a man; the minor exempt); the exam's person the stubborn and rebellious daughter — exempt")
        return out("a son, not a daughter (21:18) — from two hairs until the beard rounds; a son and not a daughter, not a man; the minor exempt (the Sifrei 218:1-3; Mishnah Sanhedrin 8:1): the stubborn and rebellious daughter exempt", ['exempt'])
    if ask == 'stubborn_and_rebellious_judged_by_his_end':
        ink('21:18, 21:20', '"STUBBORN AND REBELLIOUS" — stubborn twice in the chapter, rebellious once (the reading\'s lemma assert: the stubborn root twelve seats in the Bible); "a glutton and a drunkard" the Bible\'s one seat')
        move('the Sifrei 218:4-5, 220:3 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 8:5 (the exam row, read whole)', "'STUBBORN' — a fool; 'REBELLIOUS' — a heretic (218:4); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 8:5: THE STUBBORN AND REBELLIOUS SON IS JUDGED BY HIS END — let him die innocent and not die guilty, for the death of the wicked is a benefit to them and a benefit to the world, and the death of the righteous a harm to them and a harm to the world; wine and sleep for the wicked a benefit to them and to the world, for the righteous a harm; the dispersal of the wicked a benefit, of the righteous a harm; the gathering of the wicked a harm, of the righteous a benefit; the quiet of the wicked a harm, of the righteous a benefit; THE CHAPTER'S CHAIN read by the spine as one story — the captive, the hated wife, the rebellious son, the hanged (218:5); not executed on the Sabbath or a festival (218:5)")
        dat("THE DATA ROW the_judged_by_his_end (Sanhedrin 8:5 — the wicked's death a benefit; the righteous' a harm); the chapter's chain a DATA row (the captive to the hanged); the exam's person the court that executes the rebellious son before his capital sin — accepted (judged by his end)")
        return out("stubborn and rebellious, judged by his end (21:18, 21:20) — a fool and a heretic; let him die innocent and not guilty; the chapter's chain one story (the Sifrei 218:4-5, 220:3; Mishnah Sanhedrin 8:5): the court that judges him by his end accepted", ['accepted'])
    if ask == 'they_chastise_him_and_he_hears_not':
        ink('21:18', '"who HEARS NOT THE VOICE OF HIS FATHER OR THE VOICE OF HIS MOTHER, and THEY CHASTISE HIM and he will not hearken to them" — "hears not" twice (21:18, 21:20 — the analogy the row names)')
        move('the Sifrei 218:6-11 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 8:3 (the exam row, read whole)', "'WHO HEARS NOT THE VOICE OF HIS FATHER AND HIS MOTHER' — the parents' pardon before the verdict (218:7 — with the sotah's (the suspected wife's) husband and the rebellious elder's court, the elder's denied by R. Judah ben Beteira, 218:8); 'AND THEY CHASTISE HIM' — LASHES BEFORE THREE (218:10-11); the lamp not lit is no rebellion — gluttony FROM STOLEN MONEY by the analogy of 'he does not heed' twice (218:9); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 8:3: stole from his father and ate on others' property — liable; from his father on his father's property, from others on others', from others on his father's — not liable, until he steals from his father and eats on others'; R. Yose ben R. Judah: until he steals from his father AND from his mother")
        dat("THE PARAMETER the_theft_condition (Sanhedrin 8:3 — from his father, eaten on others' property; R. Yose ben R. Judah both parents); the parents' pardon a DATA row; the exam's person the son warned and chastised on his first offense — flogged before three: lashes the case's own body")
        return out("they chastise him and he hears not (21:18) — the pardon before the verdict; lashes before three; the theft from his father eaten on others' property (the Sifrei 218:6-11; Mishnah Sanhedrin 8:3): the son on his first offense flogged before three", ['lashes'])
    if ask == 'his_father_and_his_mother_seize_him':
        ink('21:19-20', '"THEN HIS FATHER AND HIS MOTHER SHALL SEIZE HIM AND BRING HIM OUT to the elders of his city and to the gate of his place; and they shall say to the elders of his city: THIS SON OF OURS is stubborn and rebellious, HE HEARS NOT OUR VOICE" — "the elders of his city and the gate of his place" the Bible\'s one seat (the reading\'s formula assert); "the elders of his city" 19:12\'s and 25:8\'s formula; Onkelos "the gate of the court of his place" (the reading\'s find)')
        move('the Sifrei 219:1-4 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 8:4 (the exam row, read whole); cold_run_festivals_judges (CALL) — FJ.the_three_tiers = %s; cold_run_ordinances (CALL) — OR.courts(twenty_three) = %s' % (FJ_TIERS[1], OR_23[0]), "MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 8:4: the father wills and the mother does not, or the reverse — NOT LIABLE UNTIL BOTH WILL; R. Judah: if his mother was not fit for his father he is not made a rebellious son; THE FIVE ABILITIES from the five verbs — 'they shall seize him' not the handless, 'bring him out' not the lame, 'and say' not the mute, 'this son of ours' not the blind, 'he hears not our voice' not the deaf; they warn him before three and flog him; sinned again — JUDGED BY TWENTY-THREE, and not stoned unless the first three are present ('this son of ours' — the one flogged before you); fled before the verdict was finished and the beard rounded — exempt; after the verdict — liable (219:1-4; the three and the twenty-three by CALL — festivals_judges' tiers, ordinances' court)")
        dat("THE WRITE rebellious_son_seized_commanded — a STATUS on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DJ2); THE PARAMETER the_parents_conditions (Sanhedrin 8:4 — both will; the five abilities; the three and the twenty-three; the flight before the verdict); Onkelos's court a DATA row; the exam's person the son whose father wills and whose mother does not — exempt")
        return out("his father and his mother seize him (21:19-20) — both must will; the five abilities from the five verbs; warned and flogged before three, judged by twenty-three with the three present; the flight before the verdict exempts (the Sifrei 219:1-4; Mishnah Sanhedrin 8:4; festivals_judges' %s and ordinances' %s by CALL): THE WRITE rebellious_son_seized_commanded, a STATUS on Israel at the chapters' own day; the son whose mother does not will exempt" % (FJ_TIERS[1][0], OR_23[0]), ['rebellious_son_seized_commanded', 'exempt'])
    if ask == 'a_glutton_and_a_drunkard':
        ink('21:20', '"this son of ours is stubborn and rebellious, he hears not our voice; A GLUTTON AND A DRUNKARD" — the Bible\'s one seat (the reading\'s formula assert); Proverbs 23:20\'s "gluttons of meat" the remembrance; ONKELOS "A GLUTTON OF MEAT AND A DRINKER OF WINE" — the Mishnah\'s objects written into the verse (the reading\'s find); the tartemar named in the spine\'s own Hebrew (220:3 — the reading\'s crown)')
        move('the Sifrei 220:1-4 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 8:2 (the exam row, read whole)', "MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 8:2: FROM WHEN is he liable? from when he eats A TARTEMAR (a half-maneh weight) OF MEAT and drinks HALF A LOG (a liquid measure) OF ITALIAN WINE; R. Yose says a maneh of meat and a log of wine: TWO ARMS; ate in a company of a commandment, ate at the intercalation of the month, ate second tithe in Jerusalem — not liable; ate carrion, torn flesh, creeping things, untithed produce, first tithe whose heave offering was not taken, second tithe or consecrated food not redeemed — not liable; ate every food but not meat, drank every drink but not wine — not liable, until he eats meat and drinks wine, as it is said 'a glutton and a drunkard', and the remembrance 'be not among the drinkers of wine, among the gluttons of meat' (Proverbs 23:20 — the Writings' run citation)")
        dat("THE PARAMETER the_measures_of_meat_and_wine (Sanhedrin 8:2 — the tartemar and the half log; R. Yose's maneh and log; the exclusions); Onkelos's objects a DATA row; the exam's person the son who ate every food but not meat — exempt (not a glutton until meat and wine)")
        return out("a glutton and a drunkard (21:20) — a tartemar of meat and half a log of Italian wine, or a maneh and a log (two arms); the company of a commandment, the forbidden foods and the foods not meat excluded; Onkelos writes the objects in (the Sifrei 220:1-4; Mishnah Sanhedrin 8:2): the son who ate every food but not meat exempt", ['exempt'])
    if ask == 'all_the_men_of_his_city_stone_him':
        ink('21:21', '"AND ALL THE MEN OF HIS CITY SHALL STONE HIM WITH STONES, AND HE SHALL DIE; and you shall purge the evil from your midst, AND ALL ISRAEL SHALL HEAR AND FEAR" — "and all the men of his city shall stone him" the Bible\'s one seat; "and all Israel shall hear and fear" = 13:12\'s clause (the reading\'s find: %d tokens in order shared; %s the shared run); 21:21 shares %d with 22:21\'s stoning; the purge formula\'s FIFTH seat of nine; the two verbs of stoning — Deuteronomy\'s four seats against Leviticus\'s and Numbers\' nine, 21:21 both (seducers\' readback by CALL)' % (TWIN['21:21 vs 13:12'], SHARED(DV(21, 21), DV(13, 12)), TWIN['21:21 vs 22:21']))
        move('the Sifrei 220:4, 221:1 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 6:4 (the exam row, read whole under F9); cold_run_mekoshesh (CALL) — MK.capital_procedure(stones_and_a_stone) = %s, (mode) = %s; cold_run_seducers (CALL) — SE.the_stoning_rite = %s, SE.the_hand_first = %s, SE.the_two_verbs_of_stoning = %s; cold_run_courts_prophet (CALL) — CP.the_witnesses_hand_first = %s' % (MK_STONES[0][:40], MK_MODE[0][:20], SE_RITE[1], SE_HAND[1], SE_VERBS[:30], CP_HAND[1][:1]), "'ALL THE MEN OF HIS CITY' — a presence, not the executioners: the stones then a stone (220:4 — mekoshesh's cell by CALL: the second witness's stone, all Israel's stones; 17:7's hand of the witnesses first — courts_prophet by CALL; seducers' rite); 'PURGE THE EVIL FROM YOUR MIDST' — the formula's fifth seat of nine, as persons (Onkelos 'the doer of evil'); 'ALL ISRAEL SHALL HEAR AND FEAR' — israel_hears_and_fears ONE on israel_people (13:12's line) THE TAPE'S REFERENCE, the formula's FOURTH AND LAST seat of four (221:1); stoned TWO on the running world (the blasphemer, the wood-gatherer) UNMOVED by the line — the son's own body only")
        dat("THE WRITE rebellious_son_stoning_commanded — a STATUS on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DJ2); the exam's person the stubborn and rebellious son convicted before twenty-three with the three present — stoned by the witnesses' hand first and all the men of his city, the evil purged (the body effects reused, never a line's write)")
        return out("all the men of his city stone him (21:21) — a presence, the stones then a stone, the witnesses' hand first; the purge formula's fifth seat; hear and fear the formula's last (the Sifrei 220:4, 221:1; Mishnah Sanhedrin 6:4; mekoshesh's %s, seducers' %s and courts_prophet's %s by CALL): THE WRITE rebellious_son_stoning_commanded, a STATUS on Israel at the chapters' own day; the convicted son stoned and the evil purged" % (MK_STONES[0][:24], SE_RITE[1][0], CP_HAND[1][0]), ['rebellious_son_stoning_commanded', 'stoned', 'evil_purged_from_the_midst'])
    return 'no verdict in span', [], list(P_)


def the_hanged(case, data):
    """F9 — Deut 21:22-23 — ONE LINE hanged_burial_declared writing hanging_after_death_commanded and same_day_burial_commanded (STATUSES) and corpse_overnight_barred and land_defilement_barred (BLOCKS); the stoning house and the hanging by CALL (mekoshesh, balak), the reviler by the Name by CALL (sanctions), Genesis 9:6's blood by CALL (pre_sinai), the land's atonement DATA read (refuge); the exam rows Sanhedrin 6:3, 6:4, 6:5 read whole; the reviler's own verdict stoned, hanged and buried (the body effects reused)"""
    del P_[:]
    ask = case['ask']
    if ask == 'a_sin_worthy_of_death_and_you_hang_him':
        ink('21:22', '"AND IF A MAN HAS COMMITTED A SIN WORTHY OF DEATH, and he is put to death, AND YOU HANG HIM ON A TREE" — "a sin worthy of death" and "and you hang him on a tree" the Bible\'s one seat each; the hanging root in the Torah at 21:22-23 alone (the reading\'s lemma assert); hanged ONE on the running world (the_baker — Genesis 40:22, the Egyptians\' hanging alive) THE TAPE\'S REFERENCE; Numbers 25:4\'s hanging_commanded and Leviticus 24\'s sentence_declared and stoned_as_commanded the readback\'s REFERENCES')
        move('the Sifrei 221:1-3 (read whole at the reading); MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 6:4 (the exam row, read whole); cold_run_mekoshesh (CALL) — MK.capital_procedure(hanging) = %s; cold_run_balak (CALL) — BK.peor(hang_before_the_sun) = %s; cold_run_sanctions (CALL) — SA.curser(mode) = %s' % (MK_HANG[0][:40], BK_HANG[1], SA_MODE[0]), "MISHNAH SANHEDRIN 6:4: THE STONING HOUSE was two heights; one of the witnesses pushes him on his hips — turned on his heart he is turned back; if he died of it, done; if not, the second witness takes the stone and puts it on his heart; if he died, done; if not, his stoning is by all Israel — 'the hand of the witnesses shall be on him first, and the hand of all the people last' (17:7); ALL THE STONED ARE HANGED — R. Eliezer; THE SAGES: only the reviler and the idolater are hanged (mekoshesh by CALL — the wood-gatherer NOT hanged by the sages' arm); a man is hanged facing the people and a woman facing the tree — R. Eliezer; the sages: A MAN IS HANGED AND NOT A WOMAN; R. Eliezer: did not Simeon ben Shetach hang women in Ashkelon? they said: eighty women he hanged, and two are not judged in one day; HOW DO THEY HANG HIM? they sink the beam in the earth with the wood coming out of it, and put his hands one over the other and hang him; R. Yose: the beam leans on the wall and he hangs him as the butchers do; THEY RELEASE HIM AT ONCE, and if he stayed the night he transgresses a prohibition; Numbers 25:4's 'hang them before the sun' — the idolaters judged and hanged (balak by CALL); 'not alive as the kingdom does' (221:3)")
        dat("THE WRITE hanging_after_death_commanded — a STATUS on israel_people at the chapters' own day (DJ2); THE PARAMETERS who_is_hanged (Sanhedrin 6:4 — all the stoned or the reviler and the idolater alone; a man and not a woman) and the_hangings_form (the beam, the hands, the release at once); the exam's person the reviler stoned before the people — hanged after his death (the body effect reused; hanged 1 on the running world unmoved)")
